        "original_id": "fdd8b0f2-fd00-5460-9e37-dc6a80c3f416",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Archie Andrews, John L. Goldwater, Bob Montana, Vic Bloom, Fiona Staples\n- Companies: Archie Comics\n- Products: Archie, Archie Andrews radio series, syndicated Archie Andrews comic strip, The Archie Show, Archie's Weird Mysteries, North 40, DV8: Gods and Monsters, T.H.U.N.D.E.R. Agents, Saga\n- Topics: comic books, comic book artists\n\nFacts:\n- In 1941, publisher John L. Goldwater and artist Bob Montana created Archie Andrews in collaboration with writer Vic Bloom.\n- Archie Andrews is the main character in an American comic book series published by Archie Comics.\n- Archie Andrews is also featured in the long-running Archie Andrews radio series, a syndicated comic strip, The Archie Show, and Archie's Weird Mysteries.\n- Archie is an ongoing comic book series, also known as Archie Comics, that features the Archie Comics character Archie Andrews.\n- Fiona Staples is a Canadian comic book artist known for work on North 40, DV8: Gods and Monsters, T.H.U.N.D.E.R. Agents, Archie, and Saga.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
